Package: tabicl2synthr
Title: Synthetic Tabular Data Generation with TabICLv2
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Alexander", "Kowarik", , "alex@kowarik.net", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8598-4130")))
Description: Generates synthetic tabular data sets that mimic the structure of an
    input data set. The wrapper calls the 'TabICLUnsupervised' class of the
    Python 'tabicl' package through 'reticulate', which models the joint
    distribution of all columns as a product of conditionals using the
    pretrained TabICLv2 foundation model and draws new rows by autoregressive
    sampling. Numeric, integer, logical and categorical columns are supported
    and the original column schema is restored in the generated data.
